    <briefdescription>
<para>The templates and the concepts for extending the µTest++ testing framework. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension" kindref="compound">extension</ref></computeroutput> namespace holds what the applications use to write their own comparators, predicates, operators, and helpers, reported as the built-in ones are:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1compare__op" kindref="compound">compare_op</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1predicate__op" kindref="compound">predicate_op</ref></computeroutput> (defined in <computeroutput><ref refid="detail_8h" kindref="compound">detail.h</ref></computeroutput>), the expressions of the binary comparisons and of the unary predicates, parametrised by a tag that defines the operation and its symbol in the failure reports; they are built from the operands and a tag object, for example <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1compare__op" kindref="compound">compare_op</ref>{ lhs, rhs, my_tag{} }</computeroutput>, with the template arguments deduced, and the tag satisfies <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1compare__tag" kindref="compound">compare_tag</ref></computeroutput> (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1predicate__tag" kindref="compound">predicate_tag</ref></computeroutput> for the predicates);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the C++20 concepts with the same constraints as the framework itself: whether a type is a framework expression type (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1is__op" kindref="compound">is_op</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1any__op" kindref="compound">any_op</ref></computeroutput>), and whether it is accepted by <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput> (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1checkable" kindref="compound">checkable</ref></computeroutput>) or by the message operator (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1printable" kindref="compound">printable</ref></computeroutput>), and the constraints of the tags (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1compare__tag" kindref="compound">compare_tag</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1predicate__tag" kindref="compound">predicate_tag</ref></computeroutput>) and of the operands of the approximate comparator (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1approx__operand" kindref="compound">approx_operand</ref></computeroutput>); with the deprecated functionality enabled, they also tell whether a deprecated value wrapper carries a floating-point tolerance (<computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1has__epsilon" kindref="compound">has_epsilon</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The namespace is separate from the top namespace, so that <computeroutput>using namespace <ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref></computeroutput> does not bring these generic names into the application code; refer to them qualified, as <computeroutput>mt::extension::is_op&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
